        <body>
            <div xml:id="d400">

                <pb facs="0938" n="842" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg842"/>

                <head>No. 371.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mathews to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1879-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            5, 1879</date>. (Received July 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 322.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Sultan of Morocco has encamped with his army near Rabat, where he is expected
                    this week.</p>
                <p>He has brought under subjection during his progress the Berber tribes in the
                    province of Fedla, who have been in a state of insurrection during the last
                    twenty years. Thirty-four heads of rebels have been sent to be exposed on the
                    walls of Rabat to inspire terror among the rebel tribes of Zayr, who have been
                    committing numerous robberies and murders this year in the neighborhood of that
                    town.</p>
                <p>It is reported that the Sultan will not remain more than ten days at Rabat, but
                    will proceed without further delay to Mequinez.</p>
                <p>Sid Mohamed Bargash, the Moorish minister for foreign affairs, has engaged one of
                    the Gibraltar steamers to convey him to Rabat, having been summoned to the
                    court.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>The tribe of Angera, dwelling in the district between Tangier and Ceuta, are in a
                    state of insubordination against their governor, Kaid Kanja.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FELIX A. MATHEWS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
